<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
        item 1: Android 11+ hides other packages unless they are declared here.

        Without this, `packageManager.getPackageInfo("com.tencent.mm", 0)` throws NameNotFoundException while
        WeChat is installed and running, and the UI reported "微信未安装".

        v5.0.0: the same applies to Douyin, which is now a host. HostApp.installed() and
        HostApp.versionOf() query each host's package to list what the user actually has, so every
        package they may query must be visible here, not just the WeChat one.
    -->
    <queries>
        <package android:name="com.tencent.mm" />
        <package android:name="com.ss.android.ugc.aweme" />
        <package android:name="com.ss.android.ugc.aweme.lite" />
        <package android:name="com.ss.android.ugc.trill" />
        <!--
            v6.0.0: Soul. Same reason as the Douyin entries above: HostApp.versionOf() calls
            getPackageInfo on each host's first package, and on Android 11+ a package that is not
            declared here is INVISIBLE, so the call throws and the UI reports 「Soul 未安装」 while
            Soul is installed and running. That is the exact failure this block already prevented
            for WeChat.
        -->
        <package android:name="cn.soulapp.android" />
        <!--
            v7.0.0: Kuaishou. Same reason as the Soul entry above, which is the same reason as the
            Douyin entries before it: HostApp.versionOf() calls getPackageInfo on each host's first
            package, and on Android 11+ a package that is not declared here is INVISIBLE, so the
            call throws and the UI reports 「快手 未安装」 while Kuaishou is installed and running.
        -->
        <package android:name="com.smile.gifmaker" />
        <!--
            v8.0.0: QQ. Same reason as the Kuaishou entry above, which is the same reason as every
            entry before it: HostApp.versionOf() calls getPackageInfo on each host's first package, and
            on Android 11+ a package that is not declared here is INVISIBLE, so the call throws and the
            UI reports 「QQ 未安装」 while QQ is installed and running.

            NOTE the AndroidManifest also needs this because QQ ships sub-processes
            (com.tencent.mobileqq:video, com.tencent.mobileqq:MSF); those are processes rather than
            packages and are intentionally NOT declared here.
        -->
        <package android:name="com.tencent.mobileqq" />

        <!--
            v8.1.0: TIM, for the same reason as the QQ entry above. On Android 11+ a package that is
            not declared here is INVISIBLE to getPackageInfo, so without this line the UI would report
            「TIM 未安装」 while TIM is installed and running. TIM is the QQ host: a separate APK with
            the same NT chat engine, so it is served by the same hooks. See HostApp.QQPkgs.QQ for the
            measured evidence (the TIM 4.1.0 APK was unpacked and every hooked class was found).
        -->
        <package android:name="com.tencent.tim" />

        <!--
            v9.5.0: Xiaohongshu (小红书), for the same reason as every entry above.

            ============================== WHY THIS LINE WAS MISSING, AND WHAT IT COST ==============================

            This is the SIXTH host, and forgetting this line is the one step of adding a host that
            produces NO error anywhere, so it shipped broken in the first 9.5.0 build and the user
            reported it directly:

                「怎么推荐作用域推荐应用没有小红书了」

            On Android 11+ a package not declared here is INVISIBLE to `getPackageInfo`, and
            `HostApp.versionOf()` queries each host's first package to build the list. Without this line
            the call throws NameNotFoundException, the host is dropped from the recommendation list, and
            the app reports 「未安装」 even while 小红书 is installed and running, so the user cannot
            even SELECT it in LSPosed's scope picker, which makes every hook in this module unreachable.

            NOTE the package is `com.xingin.xhs`, the ANDROID package. The APK's internal Java classes
            live under `com.xingin.*` (for example `com.xingin.im.*`, `com.xingin.chatbase.bean.*`), but
            declaring that namespace here would be wrong: `<queries>` matches package names, and
            `com.xingin` is not a package. The clone packages follow the parent's pattern on this host
            (see HostApp.of's prefix rule).
        -->
        <package android:name="com.xingin.xhs" />
    </queries>

    <application
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:icon="@mipmap/luoliao_icon"
        android:label="落聊"
        android:roundIcon="@mipmap/luoliao_icon_round"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.LuoLiao">

        

        <activity
            android:name=".ui.SettingsActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:label="落聊"
            android:theme="@style/Theme.LuoLiao" />

        <!--
            item 1: LEGACY Xposed registration, exactly as Nuke declares it.

            Nuke ships these four meta-data entries plus assets/xposed_init, and its scope stays EDITABLE
            in LSPosed. That is how it works with an app clone. Registering the same way here gives our
            module that behaviour too, so the user can tick their clone in the scope page.

            Both registrations point at the same ModuleEntry, so whichever API LSPosed chooses, the module
            loads.
        -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="xposedmodule"
            android:value="true" />
        <meta-data
            android:name="xposedminversion"
            android:value="82" />
        <!--
            Shown in the LSPosed module list. v5.0.0: it named only 微信, so Douyin users had no way to
            know the module also serves 抖音. Both hosts are named now. v6.0.0 adds Soul, by the same
            reasoning applies a third time: a Soul user reading 「微信/抖音」 would conclude the module
            is not for them, even though it is ticked in their scope list. v7.0.0 adds 快手 for exactly
            the same reason; the list is now 微信/抖音/Soul/快手. v8.0.0 adds QQ, which is the point at
            which this list must stay accurate: it has now grown once per host, and a QQ user reading a
            description that omits QQ would uninstall the module rather than file a bug.
        -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="xposeddescription"
            android:value="落聊：长按微信 / 抖音 / Soul / 快手 / QQ / 小红书 的消息进行 AI 意图分析" />
        <meta-data
            android:name="xposedscope"
            android:resource="@array/xposed_scope" />

        <!--
            REQUIRED for libxposed remote preferences.
            Without this declaration the framework does not expose the module's
            SharedPreferences to the hooked (WeChat) process, so getRemotePreferences()
            returns nothing and the API key always reads back empty.
        -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="xposedsharedprefs"
            android:value="true" />

        <!--
            v10.1.0: 模块入口。用户要求「安装落聊桌面不会显示应用」。

            ==================== 为什么用 CATEGORY_INFO 而不是删掉 intent-filter ====================

            直接删掉 intent-filter 会让 Activity **无法被任何外部应用启动**，包括 LSPosed ——
            用户就再也进不去这个配置界面了（而且没有桌面图标可以恢复，等于把自己锁在门外）。
            所以正确做法不是"删掉入口"，而是**换一个不被桌面显示的入口类别**。

            Android 对这件事有专门的约定：CATEGORY_INFO 表示"这是这个应用的信息/设置页"，
            桌面**不会**为它创建图标，但它仍然是一个可解析的 ACTION_MAIN 入口。
            更关键的是 AOSP 的 `PackageManager.getLaunchIntentForPackage()` 实现是
            **先查 CATEGORY_INFO、查不到才退回 CATEGORY_LAUNCHER**：

                intent = new Intent(ACTION_MAIN).addCategory(CATEGORY_INFO).setPackage(pkg)
                if (queryIntentActivities(intent).size() == 0) {
                    intent = new Intent(ACTION_MAIN).addCategory(CATEGORY_LAUNCHER)...
                }

            而 LSPosed 的模块详情页正是用 getLaunchIntentForPackage 来放「打开」按钮的，
            所以这条改动的结果恰好是用户要的：**桌面没有图标，LSPosed 里还能打开**。

            exported 必须保持 true：LSPosed 是**另一个应用**，跨应用启动要求 exported。

            【兜底入口】万一某个第三方桌面仍然显示了它，或者用户需要在没有 LSPosed 的情况下进来，
            可以用 adb 直接按组件名启动（不需要 exported 之外的任何东西）：
                adb shell am start -n com.luoliaoo.wechat/.ui.LauncherActivity
        -->
        <activity
            android:name=".ui.LauncherActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:theme="@style/Theme.LuoLiao">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.INFO" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>

        <!--
            v2.5.0: lets the share sheet hand the packaged log to another app without any storage permission.

            v7.1.0 FIX (captain): the authority used to be the HARDCODED literal
            "com.luoliaoo.wechat.fileprovider". A provider authority is unique across the
            whole device, so the `debug` build (which renames the package to
            `com.luoliaoo.wechat.debug` via `applicationIdSuffix`) declared the SAME
            authority as the release build and could not be installed alongside it:

                INSTALL_FAILED_CONFLICTING_PROVIDER: provider name
                com.luoliaoo.wechat.fileprovider (in package com.luoliaoo.wechat.debug)
                is already used by com.luoliaoo.wechat

            That broke the whole point of having two flavours (the debug build with full
            logging is the one used for on-device diagnosis). `${applicationId}` resolves
            per-variant, so release keeps the old authority and debug gets
            `com.luoliaoo.wechat.debug.fileprovider`, and both install together.

            WHY THIS WAS EASY TO MISS: every OTHER package-derived value in this manifest
            is already variant-aware (e.g. the androidx.startup provider merged by the
            manifest merger takes the suffixed id automatically). Only a hand-written
            literal stays fixed, so it silently diverges the moment a suffix is added.
        -->
        <provider
            android:name="androidx.core.content.FileProvider"
            android:authorities="${applicationId}.fileprovider"
            android:exported="false"
            android:grantUriPermissions="true">
            <meta-data
                android:name="android.support.FILE_PROVIDER_PATHS"
                android:resource="@xml/luoliao_file_paths" />
        </provider>

    </application>

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" />

</manifest>
